                        "glosses": [
                            "Top; summit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "609509fc-4942-4282-bdf5-bdc344efdd73",
                                "sense_id": "976900ae-abc6-3159-b898-dee39ac5cf89",
                                "text": "the Shibboleth and Culmen of Honesty"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e44b47d-ab0c-322f-9fb5-d75ac2bce277",
                        "entry_id": "3b2aa43f-d20b-3b01-b351-1f903922e5d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The dorsal ridge of a bird's bill."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a45abf90-5106-4d2e-a505-0981e6e9ee45",
                                "sense_id": "9e44b47d-ab0c-322f-9fb5-d75ac2bce277",
                                "text": "The measurements were taken as follows: wing length, from the carpal joint to the tip of the longest primary; tarsus length, from the tibiotarsal joint to the distal undivided scute; upper mandible length, the chord length from the point where the culmen enters the feathers of the head to the tip; bill depth, in the vertical plane level at the anterior edge of the nares."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a83bb459-1054-4c38-a571-67fbd7914442",
                                "sense_id": "9e44b47d-ab0c-322f-9fb5-d75ac2bce277",
                                "text": "A very simple form was found in the carving shown in Pl. 17, fig. 13, where a long projecting knob is seen at the base of the culmen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
